{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792395110,"nonce":"e8knRr64Kya6ahzbsuYmDdmpPYU=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/53","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABYNhR4A","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"53","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"db1a1a5425e9957a6f527f3866a4bc3cb5b0a2d5a9b4edf5c1141501776c318e","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[TASK](Lint) Replace the Quasar template rules and cover the tests","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/53"},"title":"[TASK](Lint) Replace the Quasar template rules and cover the tests","message":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** replace the template ESLint config with rules we chose, and lint the tests too.\n- **Why:** the config is still the Quasar starter (with Cordova, Capacitor and Google Analytics globals), and test files are never linted.\n- **User impact:** none.\n- **Decision needed:** keep type-aware TypeScript rules or not (see below).\n- **Effort:** small.\n\n---\n\n## What we have today\n- `frontend/eslint.config.js` is still the Quasar template:\n  - Vue rules at the lowest level (`flat/essential`);\n  - globals for platforms we don't use (`ga`, `cordova`, `Capacitor`, `chrome`, `browser`), and Node globals on every file, browser code included;\n  - an override for `src-pwa/custom-service-worker.ts`, a folder that doesn't exist;\n  - an empty `ignores` block;\n  - `@vue/eslint-config-prettier/skip-formatting` for Prettier.\n- `npm run lint` only covers `src/`. The 22 files in `tests/` and the config files are never linted.\n- `npm run format` and `format:check` also only cover `src/`. The tests happen to be formatted today, but nothing keeps them that way.\n\n## Why it matters\nTemplate leftovers hide which rules the team actually chose. Unlinted tests drift: there are already 2 lint errors in `tests/`.\n\n## What we propose\n1. **Config**, as planned in #39:\n   ```js\n   js.configs.recommended,\n   pluginVue.configs['flat/recommended'],\n   vueTsConfigs.recommended, // or recommendedTypeChecked, see Decision 1\n   prettier, // eslint-config-prettier, replaces @vue/eslint-config-prettier/skip-formatting\n   ```\n   - `ignores` for `dist/`, `.quasar/` and `quasar.config.*.temporary.compiled*`;\n   - browser globals for `src/`, Node globals only for `tests/`, `quasar.config.ts` and `eslint.config.js`;\n   - drop the Cordova, Capacitor, BEX and `ga` globals and the `src-pwa` block.\n2. **Cover the tests:** `lint` becomes `eslint .`, and `format` / `format:check` run on `.` (add a `.prettierignore` if needed). Update the lefthook globs to match.\n3. **Fix the findings in the same PR:** 29 today, 17 of them auto-fixable.\n\n## Decisions needed\n1. #39 planned `vueTsConfigs.recommended`, like co2-calculator. Today we use `recommendedTypeChecked`, which also catches things like unhandled promises but is slower. Recommended: **keep `recommendedTypeChecked`** unless lint time becomes a problem.\n\n## Done when\n- [ ] `npm run lint` and `npm run format:check` cover `src/`, `tests/` and the config files, and pass.\n- [ ] No template globals and no `src-pwa` block are left in the config.\n- [ ] A lint error in a test file turns the Quality Checks PR check red.\n\n## Technical notes\n- Replaces the ESLint part of #39 (closed by #50, which delivered the quality workflow). Branch protection is out of scope for now.\n- Findings with `flat/recommended` on `src/` + `tests/`, measured on `dev` at `709194c` (2026-10-19), with `recommendedTypeChecked` still on: `vue/attributes-order` 15, `vue/require-default-prop` 6, `vue/no-template-shadow` 4, `vue/v-slot-style` 2, `@typescript-eslint/no-this-alias` 2 (both in `tests/`).\n- #42 plans to add `@intlify/eslint-plugin-vue-i18n` on top of this config.\n- Reference: `EPFL-ENAC/co2-calculator` `frontend/eslint.config.js`.","files":null}]}